{"archetypes":[{"name":"grammar-coverage","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan's tier-1 assertion grammar claims to cover all real `contains` call shapes in the repo; verify this against actual harness files to catch silent skip-coverage gaps that would make the verifier useless.","prompt_body":"Inspect every `test-*.sh` under `scripts/` and `skills/*/scripts/` for `contains` call invocations and compare their actual argument shapes and quoting styles against the tier-1 grammar the plan specifies (`contains \"$VAR\" 'literal' 'label'`). Also enumerate every target-file assignment form used in those harnesses (e.g., `SUBJECT=`, `SKILL_MD=`, `FILE=`, `TARGET=`) and check whether the plan's backward-scan heuristic — resolving `VAR=\"$REPO_ROOT/...\"` and `VAR=\"$SCRIPT_DIR/../...\"` — actually covers them. If real assignment forms exist that the heuristic cannot resolve, those assertions silently become `UNRESOLVED_VAR` warnings, and high-value pins against frequently-edited files will never be checked — a structural gap in the plan's protection. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"insertion-point-fidelity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan makes specific structural claims about variable names, function names, and case-arm neighbors inside `relevant-checks.sh`; any mismatch means the plan's diff will silently mis-apply or break the script.","prompt_body":"Read `scripts/relevant-checks.sh` in full and verify each structural anchor the plan relies on: that `run_direct_relevant_targets()` exists with a `case \"$f\"` block containing arms named `test-background-monitor-wait` and `test-collect-agent-results` adjacent to the planned insertion point; that `MODIFIED_FILES` is in scope as a shell variable at the location where the pin-phase block is to be inserted; that `run_post_checks` is a callable function invoked after the direct-targets block; and that `PHASES_RUN` is already incremented elsewhere so the new `PHASES_RUN=$((PHASES_RUN + 1))` line is coherent. Also check whether the plan's `printf '%s\n' \"$MODIFIED_FILES\"` idiom is correct given how `MODIFIED_FILES` is actually populated (array, newline-delimited string, or space-delimited string). Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"makefile-shard-audit","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan asserts `test-harnesses-3` is the lightest shard with exactly 2 current targets and that the master aggregate is at line 47; wrong shard routing or a stale line-number claim causes a diff that lands in the wrong place or unbalances CI.","prompt_body":"Read the `Makefile` and enumerate which targets are currently listed under each `test-harnesses-N` shard, then verify the plan's claim that `test-harnesses-3` is the lightest shard with only 2 targets. Also verify the plan's claim that the master `test-harnesses:` aggregate target is at line 47 and that the `.PHONY` declaration at line 4 is where the new target should be inserted. If the shard is heavier than claimed, adding `test-check-contains-pins` there may further unbalance CI rather than balance it. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
